<report>
<title>Unpaired t test</title>
<line></line>
<line>Mean of <in>title_0</in> = <inu>mean_0</inu>  (n = <in>n0</in>)</line>
<line>Mean of <in>title_1</in> = <inu>mean_1</inu>  (n = <in>n1</in>)</line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Assuming equal variances</u></line>
<line>Combined standard error = <inu>error</inu></line>
<line>df = <in>df</in></line>
<line>t =  <inu>t</inu></line>
<line><pval>One sided <inp>p_1</inp></pval></line>
<line><pval>Two sided <inp>p_2</inp></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for difference between means = <inu>from</inu> to <inu>to</inu></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>Power <in>pwr</in></line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Assuming unequal variances</u></line>
<line>Combined standard error = <inu>error_unequal</inu></line>
<line>df = <inu>df_unequal</inu></line>
<line>t(d) =  <inu>t_unequal</inu></line>
<line><pval>One sided <inp>p_1_unequal</inp></pval></line>
<line><pval>Two sided <inp>p_2_unequal</inp></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line><ci><in>pc_unequal</in>% confidence interval for difference between means = <inu>from_unequal</inu> to <inu>to_unequal</inu></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>Power <in>pwr_unequal</in></line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Comparison of variances</u></line>
<line><in>say1</in></line>
<line><in>say2</in></line>
</report>
